es for two RecA homologs in promoting meiotic chromosome synapsis.</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>2684</fpage><lpage>2695</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7590245</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000858-Henning1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henning</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturzbecher</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Homologous recombination and cell cycle checkpoints: Rad51 in tumour progression and therapy resistance.</article-title><source>Toxicology</source><volume>193</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14599770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000858-Thorslund1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thorslund</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Esashi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>West</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Interactions between human BRCA2 protein and the meiosis-specific recombinase DMC1.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>2915</fpage><lpage>2922</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17541404</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000858-Story1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Story</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Steitz</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Structure of the recA protein-ADP complex.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>355</volume><fpage>374</fpage><lpage>376</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1731253</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000858-Shin1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group 